-- Criminal Law (Temporary Provisions) Act 1955, ss 1, 6 to 13, 16, 18, 21, 27, 27A, 30, 31, 35, 44 -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked
-- against a decided case or subsidiary legislation (none was retrieved).
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which flags are set (scratchpad gen_criminal-law-temporary-provisions-act-1955.py). Expected results were written by
-- hand from the text.

`bank strike on 20 days' proper notice` MEANS Stoppage WITH
    `kind` IS `a strike`
    `service` IS `banking services`
    `days of notice` IS 20
    `signatories` IS 7
    `signed by the employer` IS FALSE
    `delivered as required` IS TRUE
    `starts before the date in the notice` IS FALSE
    `proceedings pending` IS FALSE
    `in answer to an illegal stoppage by the other side` IS FALSE

